N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): No source plate exists because this is a new composition. Bar-by-bar audit: bars 1-2 the Guitar ground alone (D3 quarter, F3 eighth, A3 dotted quarter, G3-F3 eighths | D3 quarter, G3 eighth, B3 dotted quarter, A3-G3 eighths), Voice rests; bars 3-4 the ground again under the Voice's D5 dotted quarter, C5 eighth, A4 half | B4 quarter, C5-B4 eighths, G4 half; bar 5 Voice A4 quarter, C5-D5 eighths, E5 and D5 quarters over a whole-bar D3; bar 6 Voice rests, Guitar answers A3 quarter, C4 eighth, D4 dotted quarter, C4-A3 eighths; bar 7 Voice B4 quarter, A4-G4 eighths, F4 and E4 quarters, Guitar dyads G3+D4, F3+C4, E3+B3, D3+A3, C3+G3 in the same rhythm; bar 8 Voice D4 whole, Guitar D3+A3 whole. Every bar of both parts totals eight eighths. Voice range D4-E5, largest leap a major third (B4-G4, bar 4); Guitar range C3-D4. Vertical check: on beats 1-3 the Voice sits an octave, sixth, third or their compounds above the Guitar; on beat 4 of bars 3 and 4 the ground's passing G3 and A3 make a brief ninth (A4 over G3) and seventh (G4 over A3) under the held voice note, resolving on the next eighth. The batch draft was one unaccompanied line that claimed mono-, homo- and polyphony and dialogue without a second part. Originality check: neither line is the vocal, guitar riff or ostinato of "Ai Du" or of other Touré recordings checked ("Diaraby", "Bonde", "Savane"); a Dorian ground built on D is common property. The analyzer reads only the Voice line and places it in Grade 5 (dotted quarter and eighth, two parts); the Grade 8 concepts, the textures and the mode, live in how the two parts combine, which it does not read.
N:UNCERTAIN: Whether students name the textures by ear in so short a piece, whether the ground's late dotted quarter feels steady at quarter note = 72-92, and whether the title's "Sahel" suggests a Malian style the piece does not have have not been settled. A Malian/Songhai music educator must review the framing; a classroom trial, a second score reader and a student listening panel remain required before publication.
